####################################################################################################################################
# A .gitignore file specifies intentionally untracked files that Git shouldn't track by default. Each line in a .gitignore file    #
# specifies a pseudo-regex pattern. Any file with path and name matching the pattern is not tracked by default, although you can   #
# still manually add and track ignored files.                                                                                      #
#                                                                                                                                  #
# Full documentation about .gitignore: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitignore                                                          #
#                                                                                                                                  #
# There is a Github repository with a collection of gitignore templates that provide a starting point to assemble a full project   #
# .gitignore: https://github.com/github/gitignore                                                                                  #
#                                                                                                                                  #
# We generally add sets of patterns in sections according to the kinds of unwanted cruft that are created by different language    #
# tools, IDEs, editors, generators, and operating systems. The templates above are a good starting point for each section.         #
####################################################################################################################################


####################################################################################################################################
###                                                             Yarn                                                             ###
####################################################################################################################################

# Yarn package manager for Node.js. Yarn provides fast, reliable, and secure dependency management and project tool scripting. We
# use it in every project (regardless of other ecosystems also in use) to provide a consistent developer interface for the project.

# Plug'n'Play (PnP) is a feature of Yarn that eliminates the need for a node_modules folder. It uses only one `.pnp.cjs` file.
.pnp.*

# Other configuration goes into the `.yarn/` directory. Some but not all of the stuff in `.yarn/` should be ignored.
# https://yarnpkg.com/getting-started/qa#which-files-should-be-gitignored
.yarn/*
!.yarn/cache
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/sdks
!.yarn/versions

# Misc cruft that Yarn might create in the project root.
.yarn-integrity
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Lockfiles and config should always be committed.
!yarn.lock
!.yarnrc
!.yarnrc.yml


####################################################################################################################################
###                                                           Secrets                                                            ###
####################################################################################################################################

# Various secrets and sensitive information that should not be committed to a repository.

# DotEnv environment variable files.
# https://www.dotenv.org/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# GPG private keys.
# https://www.gnupg.org/
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/GPG.gitignore
secring.*

# PuTTY private keys.
# https://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/putty/
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/PuTTY.gitignore
*.ppk

# SSH/certificate private keys
# https://www.openssh.org/
.ssh/
id_rsa
*.pem
*.key


####################################################################################################################################
###                                                   AI Agents and Assistants                                                   ###
####################################################################################################################################

# Common agent instruction and project configuration files that should not be committed or shared with the project team.

# Aider
# https://aider.chat/
.aider.input.history
.aider.chat.history.md
.aider.llm.history
.aider.tags.cache.v*
.aiderignore

# Claude Code
# https://code.claude.com/
.claudeignore
.claude/*.local.json
./**/CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/**/*.log

# Cursor
# https://cursor.com/
.cursorignore
.cursorindexingignore

# Gemini CLI
# https://gemini.google.com/
gemini-debug.log
.gemini-clipboard/

# OhMyOpenAgent
# https://omo.dev/
.sisyphus/*
!.sisyphus/rules/


